class.description:
An [InputActions] resource holds a list of [InputAction]s whose names are unique. The [InputMap] references two of them as its layers ([method InputMap.get_input_actions]), and it is the settings resource of [InputMapSettingsServer]. It emits [signal Resource.changed] when its list or one of its actions changes. Adding an action with a name that is already in the list replaces the old one in its place. Looking up an action by name is fast, also for hundreds of actions.
The list is the typed array [member actions], so it can be edited in the Inspector and saved as [code].tres[/code], JSON, INI or CSV (one row per action).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var actions = InputActions.new()
var jump = InputAction.new()
jump.action = &"jump"
jump.bindings = "Key:Space; JoypadButton:A"
actions.add_action(jump)
InputMap.set_input_actions(actions)
print(actions.has_action(&"jump")) # Prints true
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var actions = new InputActions();
var jump = new InputAction();
jump.Action = "jump";
jump.Bindings = "Key:Space; JoypadButton:A";
actions.AddAction(jump);
InputMap.Singleton.SetInputActions(actions);
GD.Print(actions.HasAction("jump")); // Prints True
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
